              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to make sure, then the Persian for apparently."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ای کاش",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ای کاش (ey kâsh) — \"if only, I wish\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ای کاش وقت بیشتری داشتم. ey kâsh vaqt-e bishtari dâshtam. If only I had more time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes the past for a wish about now: ey kâsh dâshtam. Kâsh alone means the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ای کاش (ey kâsh) is native Persian, built from ey \"oh\", the calling word, + kâsh \"would that\". The origin of kâsh is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
